SU(2) normalized-dimension cone invariance audit

COMMAND
make -f Makefile.research analyze_su2_normalized_dimension_invariance
./analyze_su2_normalized_dimension_invariance 50 200 1

OUTPUT
DETAIL factor=1 column=0 numerator=[2,2,7] denominator=3
DETAIL factor=1 column=1 numerator=[2,29,34,27] denominator=15
DETAIL factor=1 column=2 numerator=[7,34,89,82,55] denominator=35
DETAIL factor=1 column=3 numerator=[0,27,82,173,146,91] denominator=63
DETAIL factor=1 column=4 numerator=[0,0,55,146,281,226,135] denominator=99
SU2_NORMALIZED_DIMENSION_INVARIANCE maximum_factor=50 maximum_column=200 columns=10050 coefficient_checks=1527600 coefficient_failures=0
FIRST_FAILURE factor=-1 column=-1 row=-1 value=0

METHOD
Write d_t=2t+1 and h_t=d_(t+1)m_t-d_t m_(t+1).  The finite cone h>=0
has extreme rays

  v_x^(s)=d_x 1_(x<=s),

up to the positive denominator d_s d_(s+1).  For every q<=50 and
s<=200, the analyzer multiplies v^(s) by

  chi_q^2=sum_(a=0)^(2q) chi_a

using ordinary Clebsch--Gordan intervals.  It then evaluates every
output margin h'_t exactly.  The displayed numerator is the complete
margin vector for the selected small columns; its denominator is the
positive extreme-ray normalization.  The scan finds no negative
coefficient.  This is bounded evidence for the explicit unbounded
three-integer inequality H_(q;s,t)>=0, not its proof.

COMPILER FLAGS
g++ -O2 -std=c++20 -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Wconversion \
  -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror \
  analyze_su2_normalized_dimension_invariance.cpp \
  -o analyze_su2_normalized_dimension_invariance

